# The harness's `screendump:` end to end until M8's TUI has its own
# (docs/design.md, "The harness"): QMP's screendump, QEMU's PPM, the PNG
# and the exact comparison with tests/qemu/golden/ovmf.png. The release
# kernel boots `test=release`, whose root task waits for a line, so the
# screen holds still while it is taken: q35's std VGA at the 1280x800 OVMF
# picks from its EDID, showing what OVMF left there, TianoCore's logo and
# its two BdsDxe lines, since nothing after the firmware draws yet (the
# loader writes only COM1). OVMF's text is drawn as its lines reach COM1,
# so a screendump taken before the loader starts can catch it part drawn;
# this one comes long after. The rest is release.scenario's run, shortened.
kernel: release
cmdline: test=release
exit: success
expect: loader: GOP framebuffer 1280x800
expect: entering kernel
expect: release: type a line
screendump: ovmf
send: release input\r          # the line root checks for
expect: release: read "release input"
expect: TEST PASS
